# The blobs here are LF. A Windows checkout with core.autocrlf=true turns them into CRLF, and bash then reads the
# carriage return as part of the command: every .sh fails with "$'\r': command not found". These three lines say
# "LF, whatever the machine" for the files that get executed, and leave the rest to each person's own git settings.
*.sh text eol=lf
gradlew text eol=lf
*.py text eol=lf

# Windows runs .bat through cmd, which wants its own endings.
*.bat text eol=crlf

# Never let a converter touch a binary.
*.jar binary
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.webp binary
*.ttf binary
*.apk binary
